==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rin.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃er-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|rinnen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rinnan||to run}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*rinnaną||to run}}. More at {{m|en|run}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|~s|~ning|ran|run}}

# {{lb|en|ambitransitive|dialectal}} To [[run]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1836|author={{w|Allan Cunningham (author)|Allan Cunningham}}|title=Lord Roldan|volume=1|publisher=John Macrone|pageurl=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=UgktAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA314&dq=%22rinning%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwii76DYzsXtAhV0yjgGHYp6DYEQ6AEwAXoECAQQAg#v=onepage&q=%22rinning%22&f=false|page=314
|passage="Besides," he continued, "I'm no sure that I'm right in '''rinning'''—'''rinning'''! I'm no '''rinning''' , I'm ganging; weel then I'm no sure that I'm right doing a witch's errand, whether '''rinning''' or ganging, sae I'se stand still and consider it.{{...}}."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=a. 1846|author=w:John Imlah|chapter=Where Gadie '''rins'''|year_published=1876|editor=w:James Grant Wilson|title=The Poets and Poetry of Scotland, Volume II|publisher=w:Harper & Brothers|pageurl=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=JHdIAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA211&dq=%22rins%22%7C%22rinned%7C%22%7C%22rinning%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwj3u76WuMXtAhV1yDgGHXlGCPwQ6AEwE3oECEIQAg#v=onepage&q=%22rins%22%7C%22rinned%7C%22%7C%22rinning%22&f=false|page=211
|passage=O! gin I were where Gadie<sup>[the name of a rivulet]</sup> '''rins''',}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col|en|rinner}}

===Etymology 2===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ja|-}} {{ja-r|厘|りん}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|*}}

# A [[coin]] worth {{frac|1|1000}} of a Japanese [[yen]], no longer in [[circulation]].

